grainy-geometry ports, from the Python Grainy oracle, the parts of third-party libraries that the oracle's
geometry stage relies on for its exact pixels:

* Pillow 12.3.0 (https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow), `Image.rotate`/`Image.transform` and
  `src/libImaging/Geometry.c` (`affine_transform`, `ImagingGenericTransform`, the BICUBIC filter for float32
  images): ported to src/pillow.rs. Pillow is distributed under the MIT-CMU (HPND) licence reproduced below.
* numpy 2.5.3 (BSD-3-Clause): the behaviour of `SeedSequence`, `PCG64`, `Generator.choice` and pairwise
  summation is re-implemented in src/rng.rs and src/numeric.rs from their documented algorithms.
* OpenCV primitives come from the grainy-imgproc crate (see its NOTICE).

No lensfun code or data is included: lens corrections are supplied by the caller through `LensModel`.

